{"id":"p06-l03","minutes":40,"summary":"Interlocks and decoders are Boolean functions, and fewer gates means cheaper, faster, easier-to-check logic. You use De Morgan’s laws, minimise with Karnaugh maps, implement Quine-McCluskey, and check every minimised expression against its truth table.","html":"<h2 id=\"boolean-algebra\">Boolean algebra</h2>\n<p>Variables are 0 or 1; AND is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span>, OR is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span>, and NOT is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. Useful identities:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span> (absorption)</li>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span> (the combining rule behind every minimisation)</li>\n<li><strong>De Morgan</strong>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0019em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8352em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0019em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. Any function can be built from NAND gates alone (or NOR alone), which is how standard cell libraries work (lesson 4).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Any function can be written as a <strong>sum of products</strong> (SOP), an OR of AND terms. Each input row where the output is 1 is a <strong>minterm</strong>; for four inputs ABCD, minterm 13 is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"karnaugh-maps\">Karnaugh maps</h2>\n<p>A K-map arranges the truth table so that neighbouring cells differ in exactly one variable. Rows and columns follow Gray code (00, 01, 11, 10), and the edges wrap around. Any rectangle of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> adjacent 1s combines (by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span>) into a single product term missing <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span> variables. To minimise:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Cover every 1 with the largest possible power-of-two rectangles (<strong>prime implicants</strong>).</li>\n<li>Take the ones that are the only cover for some 1 (<strong>essential</strong> primes).</li>\n<li>Cover what’s left with as few extra primes as possible.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Don’t-care</strong> cells (input combinations that can’t happen) can be counted as 1 when that makes a group bigger.</p>\n<p><strong>Quine-McCluskey</strong> is the same idea as an algorithm: merge terms that differ in one bit, repeat until nothing merges (these are the prime implicants), then solve the covering problem. K-maps stop being practical beyond five or six variables; the algorithm doesn’t.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"kmap\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>A 4-variable K-map. Tap cells to set minterms; the coloured outlines are the chosen groups, and the readout shows the minimal sum of products.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>A press may run (F = 1) only in these input states (A guard closed, B two-hand button, C maintenance key, D power OK), given as minterms {1, 3, 5, 7, 13, 15}.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Minterms 1, 3, 5 and 7 all have <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>: a group of four, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Minterms 5, 7, 13 and 15 all have <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Both groups are essential, and together they cover everything: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8352em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0019em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Six 4-input AND terms shrink to one AND and one OR (or 2 gates in factored form). Checking all 16 input rows confirms it.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">quine_mccluskey.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">from</span> itertools <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> combinations, product\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">combine</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">a, b</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;Terms are strings over {&#x27;0&#x27;,&#x27;1&#x27;,&#x27;-&#x27;}; merge if they differ in exactly one fixed bit.&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    diff = [i <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> i, (x, y) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">enumerate</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">zip</span>(a, b)) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> x != y]\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(diff) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;-&quot;</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> (a[diff[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]], b[diff[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]]):\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> a[: diff[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]] + <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;-&quot;</span> + a[diff[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> :]\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-literal\">None</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">covers</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">term, m, n</span>):\n    bits = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">format</span>(m, <span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;0<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{n}</span>b&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">all</span>(t <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;-&quot;</span> + b <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> t, b <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">zip</span>(term, bits))\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">minimise</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">ones, n, dont_care=(<span class=\"hljs-params\"></span>)</span>):\n    terms = {<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">format</span>(m, <span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;0<span class=\"hljs-subst\">{n}</span>b&quot;</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">set</span>(ones) | <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">set</span>(dont_care)}\n    primes = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">set</span>()\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">while</span> terms:\n        merged, used = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">set</span>(), <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">set</span>()\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> a, b <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> combinations(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sorted</span>(terms), <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>):\n            c = combine(a, b)\n            <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> c:\n                merged.add(c); used |= {a, b}\n        primes |= terms - used\n        terms = merged\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># cover: essential primes first, then greedy</span>\n    left, chosen = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">set</span>(ones), []\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sorted</span>(ones):\n        cands = [p <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> p <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> primes <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> covers(p, m, n)]\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(cands) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> cands[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> chosen:\n            chosen.append(cands[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>])\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> p <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> chosen:\n        left -= {m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> left <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> covers(p, m, n)}\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">while</span> left:\n        best = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(primes, key=<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> p: <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>(covers(p, m, n) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> left))\n        chosen.append(best); left -= {m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> left <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> covers(best, m, n)}\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sorted</span>(chosen)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">evaluate</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">terms, m, n</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">any</span>(covers(t, m, n) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> t <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> terms)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    f = minimise([<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">7</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">13</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">15</span>], <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;F =&quot;</span>, f)                                        <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># &#x27;0--1&#x27; is A&#x27;D, &#x27;-1-1&#x27; is BD</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> f == [<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;-1-1&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;0--1&quot;</span>]\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># De Morgan for all inputs</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> a, b <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> product((<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>), repeat=<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>):\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> (<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> (a <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> b)) == ((<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> a) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">or</span> (<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> b)) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> (<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> (a <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">or</span> b)) == ((<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> a) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> (<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> b))\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># random functions: the minimised form always matches the truth table</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> random\n    random.seed(<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> _ <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">300</span>):\n        ones = [m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> random.random() &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>]\n        terms = minimise(ones, <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">all</span>(evaluate(terms, m, <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>) == (m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> ones) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>))\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># don&#x27;t-cares can shrink the answer: BCD digits 10..15 never occur</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> minimise([<span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">9</span>], <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>, dont_care=<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>)) == [<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;1---&quot;</span>]</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Minimise <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop op-symbol small-op\" style=\"position:relative;top:0em;\">∑</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">6</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>All four have <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>, and the K-map wraps, so they form one group: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Express <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8352em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span></span></span></span> using only NAND gates.</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">F</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0019em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">((</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> by De Morgan: two NANDs for the products, one NAND to combine them, and one NAND with tied inputs to make <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7519em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. Four NAND gates.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p06-l03\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"boolean-algebra","title":"Boolean algebra"},{"id":"karnaugh-maps","title":"Karnaugh maps"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p06-l03-q1","type":"mc","q":"<p>De Morgan’s law says (AB)′ equals…</p>\n","explain":"<p>NOT-AND is OR of NOTs.</p>\n","options":["A′B′","A′ + B′","A + B","(A + B)′"],"answer":1},{"id":"p06-l03-q2","type":"mc","q":"<p>Minimal SOP for minterms {1, 3, 5, 7, 13, 15} of ABCD?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Two groups of four.</p>\n","options":["A′D + BD","ABD + A′D","D","A′B′D + BD"],"answer":0},{"id":"p06-l03-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>How many variables does a group of 4 cells remove from a product term?</p>\n","explain":"<p>A group of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> cells removes <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span> variables.</p>\n","answer":2,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p06-l03-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>K-map rows and columns are ordered in Gray code so that…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Adjacency equals a one-bit difference.</p>\n","options":["the map is sorted numerically","neighbouring cells differ in exactly one variable","don’t-cares are grouped","the map has fewer cells"],"answer":1},{"id":"p06-l03-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>How many minterms does a 4-input function have in total?</p>\n","explain":"<p>One per input combination.</p>\n","answer":16,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p06-l03-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>An essential prime implicant is one that…</p>\n","explain":"<p>It must appear in every minimal cover.</p>\n","options":["covers the most minterms","is the only prime covering some minterm","contains a don’t-care","has no complemented variables"],"answer":1}],"code":[{"file":"quine_mccluskey.py","lang":"python","src":"from itertools import combinations, product\n\ndef combine(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Terms are strings over {'0','1','-'}; merge if they differ in exactly one fixed bit.\"\"\"\n    diff = [i for i, (x, y) in enumerate(zip(a, b)) if x != y]\n    if len(diff) == 1 and \"-\" not in (a[diff[0]], b[diff[0]]):\n        return a[: diff[0]] + \"-\" + a[diff[0] + 1 :]\n    return None\n\ndef covers(term, m, n):\n    bits = format(m, f\"0{n}b\")\n    return all(t in \"-\" + b for t, b in zip(term, bits))\n\ndef minimise(ones, n, dont_care=()):\n    terms = {format(m, f\"0{n}b\") for m in set(ones) | set(dont_care)}\n    primes = set()\n    while terms:\n        merged, used = set(), set()\n        for a, b in combinations(sorted(terms), 2):\n            c = combine(a, b)\n            if c:\n                merged.add(c); used |= {a, b}\n        primes |= terms - used\n        terms = merged\n    # cover: essential primes first, then greedy\n    left, chosen = set(ones), []\n    for m in sorted(ones):\n        cands = [p for p in primes if covers(p, m, n)]\n        if len(cands) == 1 and cands[0] not in chosen:\n            chosen.append(cands[0])\n    for p in chosen:\n        left -= {m for m in left if covers(p, m, n)}\n    while left:\n        best = max(primes, key=lambda p: sum(covers(p, m, n) for m in left))\n        chosen.append(best); left -= {m for m in left if covers(best, m, n)}\n    return sorted(chosen)\n\ndef evaluate(terms, m, n):\n    return any(covers(t, m, n) for t in terms)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    f = minimise([1, 3, 5, 7, 13, 15], 4)\n    print(\"F =\", f)                                        # '0--1' is A'D, '-1-1' is BD\n    assert f == [\"-1-1\", \"0--1\"]\n    # De Morgan for all inputs\n    for a, b in product((0, 1), repeat=2):\n        assert (not (a and b)) == ((not a) or (not b)) and (not (a or b)) == ((not a) and (not b))\n    # random functions: the minimised form always matches the truth table\n    import random\n    random.seed(3)\n    for _ in range(300):\n        ones = [m for m in range(16) if random.random() < 0.5]\n        terms = minimise(ones, 4)\n        assert all(evaluate(terms, m, 4) == (m in ones) for m in range(16))\n    # don't-cares can shrink the answer: BCD digits 10..15 never occur\n    assert minimise([8, 9], 4, dont_care=range(10, 16)) == [\"1---\"]"}]}